***                  KAREL OLPC Utilities Keyword File
*** 
*** format: name, type, proc, flag, val1, val2
*** 
*** name is 12 char keyword
*** type is  0 = delimiters
***          1 = KAREL reserved word
***          2 = operation word
***          3 = identifier
***          4 = built in function
***          5 = system variable
***          6 = special multi char operators (KFORMAT only)
*** 
*** proc is a bit mask (KXREF only)
*** 15                 0
***  xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx
***  ^  ^ ^  ^ ^^^^ ^^^^
***  +--+ +--+ |||| |||+- scope : global=TRUE
***     |    | |||| ||+-- extrn : external=TRUE
***     |    | |||| |+--- single : effect single token=TRUE
***     |    | |||| +---- block : starts a block=TRUE
***     |    | |||+------ endb : ends a block=TRUE
***     |    | ||+------- scope_chg : scope change=TRUE
***     |    | |+-------- dummy : dummy declaration=TRUE
***     |    | +--------- def : all flag are valid=TRUE
***     |    +----------- type : type codes:
***     |                          VAR       0
***     |                          CONST     1
***     |                          ROUTINE   2
***     |                          PROGRAM   3
***     |                          INCLUDE   4
***     |                          LABEL     5
***     |                          TYPE      6
***     |                          NO_CHANGE 7
***     |                          FOREWARD  8
***     |                          ARG       9
***     |                          IMPLIED   10
***     |                          UNK       11
***     +---------------- reserved
*** 
*** flag (KFORMAT only)
***          0 = absolute indentation, val1 is current line, val2 is next line
***          1 = relative indentation, "         "           "         "
***          2 = absolute indentation if first word
***          3 = relative indentation if first word
***          16 = val1 has codes for pre and post spaces:
***                        0 = special case
***                        1 = strip prev and post spaces
***                        2 = strip prev, add post space
***                        3 = add prev, strip post space
***                        4 = add prev and post spaces
***                        5 = leave prev and post alone
***                        6 = leave prev, strip post space
***                        7 = strip prev, leave post space
***                        8 = leave prev, add post space
***                        9 = add prev, leave post space
***               val2 has codes for begin and end blocks:
***                        0 = no block
***                        1 = open block
***                        2 = close block
***          17,18,19 special case for MOVE statement
***          20 special case for ROUTINE statement
***          21 start body
*** 
*** comment lines must begin with '*** '
*** no blank lines are allowed
*** 
*** all entries except types 0 and 6 must be alphanumeric!
*** all names must start in column 1 and be no more than 12 chars
*** 
:=            0  132  16  0  0
&             0  136  16  0  0
'             0    0  16  0  0
.             0    0  16  1  0
])            0  144  16  2  2
,             0  136  16  2  0
;             0  144  16  2  0
*** none      0    0  16  3  0
*/<>@#        0    0  16  4  0
+-            0    0  16  5  0
([            0    0  16  6  1
*** none      0    0  16  7  0
*** none      0    0  16  8  0
*** none      0    0  16  9  0
*** 
*** type 6 must be arranged longest to shortest
***
>=<           6    0  16  4  0
--            6    0  16  0  0
..            6    0  16  1  0
::            6    0  16  7  0
<=            6    0  16  4  0
<>            6    0  16  4  0
>=            6    0  16  4  0
->            6    0  16  1  0
***
*** alphanumeric from here on
***
